  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The single letter amino acid codes is fairly easy to remember. In eleven cases out of twenty,&nbsp;it is just the first letter.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Natural Amino acid</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">One Letter Code</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(A)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Arginine</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(IV)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(B)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Aspartic acid</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(I)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(C)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Asparagine</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(II)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(D)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Alanine</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">(III)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table></blockquote>",
